---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';

/**
 * Titolare e impianto delle sezioni vengono dalla privacy policy di
 * bikeadventureseries.com, che è dello stesso titolare. Il contenuto NON è
 * ripreso alla lettera: quella policy descrive iscrizioni a eventi, ranking,
 * newsletter e diritto d'immagine — trattamenti che qui non esistono, perché
 * questo sito non ha nemmeno un form. Dichiarare trattamenti inesistenti in
 * un'informativa è un errore, non una cautela.
 */
const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — Tuscany Trail 365"
  description="What data this site collects, why, and the rights you have over it."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kick">Legal</div>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">What we collect, why, and what you can ask us to do about it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="small">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2 class="sec">Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is <strong>AdventureLab S.r.l.</strong>, Via Giulio
        Braga 98, 59100 Prato (PO), Italy — VAT no. 02410590976. For anything
        concerning your personal data, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.brand.email}`}>{site.brand.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">What you give us, and why</h2>
      <p>
        There is no account to create and nothing to buy on this site. Three
        forms ask for your email address, and each of them is a fair exchange we
        state upfront.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The GPX of a route.</strong> On every route page you can ask us
        to email you the GPX file. We send it to the address you give us, and
        that same address joins our mailing list — the two go together, and the
        tick box says so before you send anything. Alongside your email we store
        which route you asked for and its area, type and difficulty, so we know
        which corners of Tuscany people want to ride. Legal basis: your consent
        (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Bike rental and custom tour requests.</strong> On the
        <a href="/services/">rental &amp; tours page</a> you can describe what
        you are looking for. We process what you write to check availability
        with our partners and to answer you, and your address joins the same
        mailing list. Legal basis: your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). We may
        share the details of your request with the stay or the local partner who
        could serve it, and only with them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Leaving the list is one click.</strong> Every email we send
        carries an unsubscribe link, and you can also write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.brand.email}`}>{site.brand.email}</a>. Withdrawing
        your consent stops the emails from that moment on and does not affect
        what was lawful beforehand — the file you already received stays yours.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our mailing is handled by <strong>Brevo</strong> (Sendinblue SAS,
        France), which acts as our data processor and stores the data inside the
        European Union. We keep your contact until you unsubscribe.
      </p>
      <p>
        If instead you simply email us, we process your address and the content
        of your message for the sole purpose of replying — legal basis: our
        legitimate interest in answering someone who contacted us (Art. 6(1)(f)
        GDPR). We keep that correspondence only as long as it is useful for the
        exchange.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">What is collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Technical logs.</strong> The site is served by Cloudflare Pages.
        Like any web server, the infrastructure processes your IP address, the
        requested page, the time of the request, your browser and operating
        system. This is necessary to deliver the pages and to protect the site
        from abuse (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare acts as our data processor.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4 — only if you accept.</strong> We use GA4 to
        understand how many people reach the site and which pages they read.
        It runs in Google Consent Mode v2 with every storage category denied by
        default: until you press <em>Accept</em> on the banner, no analytics
        cookie is written and no measurement identifier is stored on your
        device. The legal basis is your consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), and you can
        withdraw it at any time — see the <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>.
        We do not use GA4 for advertising or profiling: ad storage, ad user data
        and ad personalisation are all left denied.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google Ireland Limited acts as our data processor for GA4. Analytics
        data may be transferred outside the European Economic Area under the
        safeguards described in Google's own privacy documentation. GA4 data is
        retained for the period configured in the property (by default, 14
        months).
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">Links that leave this site</h2>
      <p>
        The accommodation buttons send you to <strong>Stay22</strong> or to the
        property's own website. Some of those links are affiliate links — we
        explain exactly which ones, and why, in our
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>. The route
        buttons send you to <strong>Ride with GPS</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once you follow one of those links you are on someone else's site, and
        their privacy policy applies — not ours. We do not receive your personal
        data back from them: what reaches us is, at most, aggregate commission
        reporting with no information that identifies you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Articles 15 to 22 GDPR you may ask us for access to your personal
        data, and for its rectification or erasure; you may ask us to restrict
        or object to a processing operation; and you may ask for your data in a
        portable format. Where processing rests on your consent, you can
        withdraw it at any time without affecting what was lawful beforehand.
      </p>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.brand.email}`}>{site.brand.email}</a> and
        we will reply within one month. In practice, since we hold almost
        nothing about you, most requests are answered in a line or two. If you
        believe your data has been mishandled you also have the right to lodge a
        complaint with the Italian supervisory authority
        (<em>Garante per la protezione dei dati personali</em>, garanteprivacy.it)
        or with the authority of the country where you live.
      </p>

      <h2 class="sec" style="margin-top:34px">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes we update the date at the top of the page. Should
        a change affect a processing operation that rests on your consent, we
        will ask for that consent again.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
